{
  "modules": [
    {
      "id": 1017506837361886,
      "plugin": "StochasticTelegraph",
      "model": "Fermata",
      "version": "2.0.28",
      "params": [],
      "data": {
        "text": "QUIRTRACTOR\n===========\n\nThis is your basic steparound-style S&H pair except equipped with a feedback circuit, so that the CV out also controls the sawtooth oscillator rate. All kinds of patterns appear and disappear. \n\nL-R:\n\nFUNCs control pace of trigger and ramp LLFOs\n\nLLFO #1 produces pulses\n\nPULSESES divide these pulses and sends triggers to S&Hs\n\nS&H #1 samples output of LLFO #2 and passes it to VCA #2 for attenuation\n\nVCA #1 displays the present voltage from S&H #1\n\nVCA #2 attenuates voltage from S&H #1 for return to LLFO #2 v/oct input \n\nLLFO #2 makes sawtooth waves for sampling, and modulates itself (with some chaperoning)\n\nS&H #2 samples LLFO #2's sawtooth for output as CV\n\nVCA #3 shows us what's coming out the nozzle\n\nMULT outputs ",
        "width": 3,
        "screen_colors": 281200098803712,
        "font_choice": "res/fonts/ShareTechMono-Regular.ttf",
        "visible_lines": 28,
        "title_text": "QUIRTRACTOR"
      },
      "pos": [
        25,
        0
      ]
    },
